/**
 * The official PIT-11 (29) and PIT-4R (13) forms — the printed blanks a payer's
 * return is drawn onto (see pitPdf.ts).
 *
 * Source: podatki.gov.pl → PIT → Formularze PIT → "do druku" files (the page as
 * of 9.10.2026). These are flat PDFs — no XFA, no AcroForm — so they can be
 * filled in by code. Only the pages that carry the form are embedded; the
 * pages of explanatory notes that follow it are dropped, as they have no fields.
 *   PIT-11 (29)  pit-11_-29-11.pdf  (https://www.podatki.gov.pl/media/kgpgdkvp/pit-11_-29-11.pdf)
 *                4 pages, portrait; pages 1-3 embedded (A-I), page 4 is "Objaśnienia"
 *                SHA-256 of the original download:
 *                9bd660e181099569faca874ebfa2806ea18d8478e7f038a0a9555089a8c7c8ad
 *   PIT-4R (13)  pit-4r__-13-10.pdf (https://www.podatki.gov.pl/media/upwdj4jg/pit-4r__-13-10.pdf)
 *                3 pages, portrait; all embedded (the notes share page 3 with parts F, G)
 *                SHA-256 of the original download:
 *                7d030ddd48179e31f8ed137dd24673fef923ceb5b83f4db7fda5b12b0c1ca3ef
 * Forms of the rozporządzenie MF on PIT-11 / PIT-4R as in force for the income
 * of 2024 and later (e-Deklaracje schemas 4-0E and 1-0E). A new version of a
 * form needs a new layout map in pitLayout.ts, not just new bytes here.
 */

